config.cavesandcliffsbackport.dripstone=Dripstone
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.dripstone.tooltip=Dripstone, pointed dripstone, the lava cauldron and dripstone caves.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush=Lush Caves
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.tooltip=Moss, azalea, cave vines and glow berries, dripleaf, spore blossoms, glow lichen, rooted dirt, hanging roots and lush caves.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow=Powder Snow
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.tooltip=Powder snow, freezing, the powder snow bucket and cauldron.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.candles=Candles
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.candles.tooltip=Candles and candle cakes.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid=Glow Squid
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.tooltip=Glow squid, glow ink sacs and glow item frames.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls=Axolotls
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.tooltip=Axolotls and the bucket of axolotl.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats=Goats
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.tooltip=Goats and screaming goats.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks=Other Blocks and Items
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.tooltip=The light block, the Caves & Cliffs advancement and small 1.17 changes to shovels, shulkers, mob drops, pufferfish, llamas and infested blocks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music=Music
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.tooltip=1.18's music and the Otherside music disc.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.caves=Cave Regions
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.caves.tooltip=Where lush and dripstone caves are: the regions the cave streams decorate.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height=World Height
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.tooltip=1.18's world height, y -64 to 319, for new worlds of the Caves & Cliffs world type.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes=Other Changes
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.tooltip=1.17 and 1.18's changes to how existing mobs, experience orbs and mineshafts behave.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.enabled.tooltip=Deepslate, its stairs, slabs and walls, calcite, tuff, smooth basalt, the deepslate ores and raw iron and gold. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.rawOreDrops=Raw ore drops
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.rawOreDrops.tooltip=Iron ore and gold ore drop raw iron and raw gold, as in 1.17, instead of themselves. Silk Touch still gives the ore. Off, they and the deepslate iron and gold ores drop themselves.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.generate=Generate
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.generate.tooltip=Newly generated chunks get a deepslate layer at the bottom of the world, with deepslate ores and tuff in it.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.layerTop=Layer top
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.layerTop.tooltip=The height below which stone may become deepslate. Between layerFull and this, less and less of it does.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.layerFull=Layer full
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.layerFull.tooltip=The height below which all stone becomes deepslate.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.tuff=Tuff
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.tuff.tooltip=Tuff blobs generate in the deepslate layer.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.dimensions=Dimensions
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.dimensions.tooltip=Dimensions that get the deepslate layer.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.skipWorldTypes=Skip world types
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.deepslate.skipWorldTypes.tooltip=World types (their names, as in level.dat) that never get the deepslate layer.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.enabled.tooltip=Copper ore, raw copper, the copper blocks and lightning rods. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.oxidation=Oxidation
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.oxidation.tooltip=Unwaxed copper blocks slowly oxidize: exposed, weathered, then oxidized.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.lightningRods=Lightning rods
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.lightningRods.tooltip=Lightning from thunderstorms strikes the nearest lightning rod within 128 blocks instead.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.waxItems=Wax items
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.waxItems.tooltip=Items that wax copper when used on it or crafted with it (registry names). Any item with the ore name honeycomb works too.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.generate=Generate
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.generate.tooltip=Copper ore generates in newly generated chunks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.veinsPerChunk=Veins per chunk
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.veinsPerChunk.tooltip=Copper ore veins per chunk.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.veinSize=Vein size
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.veinSize.tooltip=Blocks of copper ore per vein, at most.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.minY=Lowest height
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.minY.tooltip=Lowest height of a copper ore vein.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.maxY=Highest height
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.copper.maxY.tooltip=Highest height of a copper ore vein.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.enabled.tooltip=Amethyst blocks, buds and shards, tinted glass and the spyglass. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodes=Geodes
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodes.tooltip=Amethyst geodes generate underground in newly generated chunks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodeRarity=Geode rarity
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodeRarity.tooltip=One geode in this many chunks, on average.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodeMinY=Lowest geode height
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodeMinY.tooltip=Lowest height of a geode.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodeMaxY=Highest geode height
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.amethyst.geodeMaxY.tooltip=Highest height of a geode.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.dripstone.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.dripstone.enabled.tooltip=Dripstone blocks, pointed dripstone and the lava cauldron. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.dripstone.extraCopperVeins=Extra copper veins
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.dripstone.extraCopperVeins.tooltip=Extra tries at a copper ore vein in each newly generated chunk of a dripstone cave. 0 for none.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.enabled.tooltip=Moss, azaleas, cave vines, dripleaf, spore blossoms, glow lichen, rooted dirt and hanging roots. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.glowLichen=Glow lichen
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.glowLichen.tooltip=Glow lichen grows on cave walls in newly generated chunks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.lichenTries=Lichen tries
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.lichenTries.tooltip=How many times a chunk a glow lichen is tried underground. Most tries land in solid stone.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.azaleaTrees=Azalea trees
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.lush.azaleaTrees.tooltip=Azalea trees grow on the surface above lush caves, with rooted dirt running down to the cave.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.enabled.tooltip=Powder snow, its bucket and cauldron, and freezing. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezing=Freezing
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezing.tooltip=Entities inside powder snow freeze: after 7 seconds they take damage every 2 seconds. Off, powder snow only slows and sinks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.strayConversion=Stray conversion
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.strayConversion.tooltip=Skeletons that stay in powder snow turn into strays.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.cauldronSnow=Cauldron snow
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.cauldronSnow.tooltip=Snowfall slowly fills cauldrons under the open sky with powder snow.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.patches=Patches
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.patches.tooltip=Patches of powder snow generate in snowy high ground in newly generated chunks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.patchRarity=Patch rarity
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.patchRarity.tooltip=One chunk in this many looks for a place for a patch. Only snowy ground at or above the lowest height takes one.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.patchMinY=Lowest patch height
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.patchMinY.tooltip=Lowest height of a powder snow patch.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezeImmuneWearables=Freeze immune wearables
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezeImmuneWearables.tooltip=More items that keep their wearer from freezing, besides leather armor, as item ids. Worn as boots they also walk on powder snow.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezeImmuneMobs=Freeze immune mobs
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezeImmuneMobs.tooltip=More mobs that never freeze, besides strays, polar bears, snow golems and the wither, as entity ids.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezeHurtsExtraMobs=Freeze hurts extra mobs
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.freezeHurtsExtraMobs.tooltip=More mobs that freezing hurts five times as much, besides blazes and magma cubes, as entity ids.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.walkableMobs=Walkable mobs
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.powderSnow.walkableMobs.tooltip=More mobs that walk on powder snow, besides rabbits, endermites and silverfish, as entity ids.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.candles.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.candles.enabled.tooltip=Candles, the sixteen dyed candles and candle cakes. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.enabled.tooltip=Glow squid, glow ink sacs and glow item frames. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.spawnWeight=Spawn weight
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.spawnWeight.tooltip=How often glow squid spawn in dark water deep underground, next to other mobs' weights (vanilla: 10). 0 stops them spawning.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.glowingSigns=Glowing signs
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.glowSquid.glowingSigns.tooltip=A glow ink sac used on a sign makes its text glow; an ink sac undoes it.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.enabled.tooltip=Axolotls and the bucket of axolotl. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.spawning=Spawning
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.spawning.tooltip=Axolotls spawn naturally in lush caves, in water above clay.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.spawnCap=Spawn cap
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.spawnCap.tooltip=The most naturally spawned axolotls around one player.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.breedingItem=Breeding item
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.breedingItem.tooltip=The item axolotls breed with when the game has no bucket of tropical fish, as "mod:item" or "mod:item:metadata". With a bucket of tropical fish in the game, only that bucket works.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.huntTargets=Hunt targets
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.huntTargets.tooltip=Mobs axolotls hunt in water, then leave alone for two minutes. Mobs that are not installed are skipped.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.hostileTargets=Hostile targets
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.hostileTargets.tooltip=Mobs axolotls always attack in water. Mobs that are not installed are skipped.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.hostilesAttackAxolotls=Hostiles attack axolotls
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.axolotls.hostilesAttackAxolotls.tooltip=The mobs axolotls always attack go after axolotls too.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.enabled.tooltip=Goats. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.spawnWeight=Spawn weight
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.spawnWeight.tooltip=How often goats spawn in the biomes of spawnBiomes, next to those biomes' other animals (sheep are 12, cows 8, llamas 5). 0: goats never spawn on their own.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.spawnBiomes=Spawn biomes
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.spawnBiomes.tooltip=The biomes goats spawn in, in groups of 1 to 3, on stone, gravel, snow and packed ice.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.ramming=Ramming
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.goats.ramming.tooltip=Goats ram players and mobs that stand still near them. Off, goats never ram.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.enabled.tooltip=The light block, the Caves & Cliffs advancement and the small 1.17 changes below. Off, nothing is registered and none of the changes apply.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.dirtPaths=Dirt paths
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.dirtPaths.tooltip=A shovel makes a path from dirt, coarse dirt, podzol, mycelium and rooted dirt as well as from grass.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.shulkerDuplication=Shulker duplication
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.shulkerDuplication.tooltip=An open shulker hit by another shulker's bullet teleports away and may leave a new shulker behind, less often the more shulkers are nearby.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.cookedMobDrops=Cooked mob drops
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.cookedMobDrops.tooltip=Zombies, husks and zombie villagers that die while burning drop baked potatoes, and polar bears and guardians cooked fish.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.pufferfishPoison=Pufferfish poison
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.pufferfishPoison.tooltip=Eating a pufferfish gives Poison II instead of Poison IV.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.peacefulLlamas=Peaceful llamas
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.peacefulLlamas.tooltip=Llamas do not spit at players in Peaceful difficulty.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.infestedBlocks=Infested blocks
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.blocks.infestedBlocks.tooltip=Infested blocks break faster with a pickaxe, and infested cobblestone takes half as long to break as cobblestone.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.enabled.tooltip=The Otherside music disc and 1.18's music. Off, nothing is registered.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.gameMusic=Game music
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.gameMusic.tooltip=The four tracks 1.18 added to the game music play among the old ones, in survival and creative: Comforting Memories, Floating Dream, Left to Bloom and One More Day.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.biomeMusic=Biome music
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.biomeMusic.tooltip=Lush caves, dripstone caves and the mountain biomes play their own selection of tracks, as in 1.18.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.menuMusic=Menu music
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.menuMusic.tooltip=The five tracks 1.18 added to the title screen music play among the old ones.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.othersideLoot=Otherside loot
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.music.othersideLoot.tooltip=The Otherside music disc is found in dungeon chests and in the chests of stronghold corridors. Takes effect when the world is next loaded.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.caves.lushRegions=Lush regions
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.caves.lushRegions.tooltip=Lush caves: moss, azaleas, cave vines, clay pools and dripleaf in some cave regions of newly generated chunks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.caves.dripstoneRegions=Dripstone regions
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.caves.dripstoneRegions.tooltip=Dripstone caves: dripstone and pointed dripstone in some cave regions of newly generated chunks.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.enabled=Enabled
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.enabled.tooltip=The Caves & Cliffs world type: an overworld from y -64 to 319, as in 1.18. The Nether and the End, and every world created before, keep y 0 to 255 for good. Removing this mod from such a world keeps everything from y 0 to 255 and loses everything below and above: the bedrock is at y -64, so the bottom of the world is then open at y 0. Refuses to turn on, and says so in the log, when Cubic Chunks, Caves Not Cliffs or Farmer's Future Delight is installed: they change the same parts of the game.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.defaultWorldType=Default world type
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.terrainThreads=Terrain threads
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.terrainThreads.tooltip=Worker threads that build the 1.18 terrain of a Caves & Cliffs world ahead of the server thread. 0: the computer's cores less two, from 1 to 6.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.newerBiomes=Newer biomes
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.newerBiomes.tooltip=New Caves & Cliffs worlds with 1.18 terrain also get the newer versions' biomes the installed backports have blocks for: 1.19's mangrove swamps and deep dark with Wild Update Backport, 1.20's cherry groves with Trails & Tales Backport, 1.21.4's pale gardens with Tricky Trials Backport, placed where those versions place them. Worlds keep the biomes they were made with.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.paleGarden1214=1.21.4 pale gardens
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.paleGarden1214.tooltip=With Tricky Trials Backport, new worlds place pale gardens as 1.21.5 and later do (the default: the newest version installed). On: as 1.21.4 does, for comparing seeds with 1.21.4. Read when a world is made.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomes=Other mods' biomes
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomes.tooltip=Other mods' overworld biomes (Biomes O' Plenty, Defiled Lands, Traverse, any in Forge's BiomeManager) generate in Caves & Cliffs worlds with 1.18 terrain: each takes the place of the 1.18 biome closest to it, in some regions, with its own top blocks, plants, trees and mobs. The log lists which takes whose place. Off, or with no such mod installed, the terrain is exactly 1.18's.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomesExcluded=Left-out modded biomes
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomesExcluded.tooltip=Biomes (modid:name) or whole mods (modid) left out of the 1.18 terrain.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomeHosts=Modded biome places
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomeHosts.tooltip=The 1.18 biome a modded biome takes the place of, where the automatic choice is wrong: modid:name=1.18 name, for example biomesoplenty:grove=forest.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomesMaxShare=Modded biome share
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomesMaxShare.tooltip=At most this percent of a 1.18 biome's regions go to the modded biomes that may take its place. Fewer when their BiomeManager weights are low against a vanilla biome's 10 (a rare modded biome stays rare).
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomeRegionSize=Modded biome region size
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.moddedBiomeRegionSize.tooltip=The size in blocks of the regions that each decide whether a 1.18 biome there is itself or a modded one.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.height.defaultWorldType.tooltip=Create World starts on the Caves & Cliffs world type, and a new server with no level-type in server.properties creates its world with it. Default stays in the list as the 1.12 terrain.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.monsterSpawnLight=Monster spawn light
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.monsterSpawnLight.tooltip=Monsters spawn only where block light is 0 (1.18), from spawners too.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.localMobCap=Per-player mob cap
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.localMobCap.tooltip=Each player has a mob cap of their own (1.18): mobs within 128 blocks of a player count toward that player's cap, and mobs spawn near a player only while that player's cap has room. The world's cap still applies.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.mineshaftSupports=Mineshaft supports
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.mineshaftSupports.tooltip=Mineshafts as 1.17 builds them: logs hold up bridges from the ground below, or a fence and chain hang them from the ceiling; cobwebs only where they touch two solid blocks; supports are not cut by other passages.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.experienceOrbs=Experience orb merging
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.experienceOrbs.tooltip=Experience orbs of the same size merge into one (1.17), which gives its experience one orb at a time, and orbs stop following players who have died.
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.snowSpawns=Rabbits and wolves on snow
config.cavesandcliffsbackport.changes.snowSpawns.tooltip=Rabbits spawn on grass blocks, snow, snow blocks and sand, wolves on grass blocks, snow and snow blocks (1.18).
